      "post_datetime": "2006-09-26T16:50:00+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Power/wavelength conversions",
      "content_md": "Some where on this site I read someone saying that they could take a power reading at one wavelength, then use a chart to find the equivalent power reading at a different wavelength, but for the life of me, I can't remember where I read that. I have a power meter that is calibrated for 633nm and I want to convert the power reading taken at this wavelength to it's equivalent at 671nm.\n\nCan anyone help me with this?\n\nThank you.",
      "signature": "",
      "attachments": [],
      "quotes": [],
      "is_first_post": true,
      "url": "https://holographyforum.org/forum/viewtopic.php?p=46879#p46879"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 46880,
